This morning I finished compiling pl7 on my Amstrad 1512 (8086, 640K,
20M hard disk). Total compilation time was about 7 hours in three
shifts - 8 minutes just for linking.

I just wanted to say how impressed I am by the development team's
work. Not only is it a superb game, but the makefile is a miracle, as
is the overlay scheme. The only thing I had to do was touch a couple
of files to stop it trying to use yacc.

Thanks for stretching my little machine to its' limits.
